Right. Third-partying is basically the same leverage pattern in another costume: let two forces reveal, weaken, commit, or shape each other, then enter where your marginal effort has the highest effect.

As an abstraction, it’s useful well beyond games:

observe interaction → let information/energy accumulate → identify asymmetry → enter at Kairos → use minimum sufficient force

The discipline is just to separate efficient timing from creating unnecessary harm or manipulation. In Pantheon terms, the valuable operator is opportunistic entry into an already-moving field, not predation for its own sake.

Same old song: don’t generate every wave; learn when to catch one.